---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../../../components/scenes/1.0/Hero";
import PrimordialTimeline from "../../../components/scenes/1.0/PrimordialTimeline";
import { findChapter, subPath, overviewPath } from "../../../data/course-nav";

const chapter = findChapter(1)!;

/* Topic cards for 1.0 → 1.4, all live by the time this lesson exists. */
const subs = [
  { id: "1.0", title: chapter.title, tag: "overview", tease: "The whole 380,000-year story — a tour of the first instants, the four forces emerging, and the moment light streamed free.", href: overviewPath(1), current: true },
  { id: "1.1", title: chapter.subs[0].title, tag: "forces", tease: "Gravity, electromagnetism, strong, weak — how one Superforce became four through cosmic phase transitions.", href: subPath("1.1") },
  { id: "1.2", title: chapter.subs[1].title, tag: "matter", tease: "The Standard Model — bricks (fermions), mortar (bosons), and the Higgs that gives them mass.", href: subPath("1.2") },
  { id: "1.3", title: chapter.subs[2].title, tag: "synthesis", tease: "Cosmic alchemy: in the first 15 minutes, the universe locked in the 75/25 hydrogen-helium ratio forever.", href: subPath("1.3") },
  { id: "1.4", title: chapter.subs[3].title, tag: "cmb", tease: "Recombination, the fog lifts, photons stretched by a factor of 1100 — the oldest light we will ever see.", href: subPath("1.4") },
];
---

<Layout
  title="1.0 — Particle Age · AST 100"
  description="The first 380,000 years — from the Planck epoch to recombination. Forces separate, particles form, the cosmos cools, and light streams free for the first time."
  current="/chapter/1/1.0"
  showBackdrop={true}
>
  <Hero client:load />

  <article class="relative max-w-[1100px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-10 pb-28">
    <div class="max-w-[68ch] mx-auto prose-cosmic">
      {/* ── Intro ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <header class="mt-24 mb-10" id="overview">
        <div
          data-fade
          class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.28em] uppercase text-plasma/80 mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"
        >
          <span class="block w-6 h-px bg-plasma/50"></span> the first second
        </div>
        <h2
          data-fade
          style="--delay: 80ms"
          class="font-serif font-medium text-white tracking-tight leading-[1.05]"
        >
          <span style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.6rem);"
            >Fifteen rewrites before t = 1 second</span
          >
        </h2>
      </header>

      <p data-fade class="dropcap">
        Most of what makes the universe interesting happens before the
        universe is a single second old. In that first second, gravity
        separates from the other three forces. Space exponentially inflates.
        Strong and electroweak forces split. Quarks freeze into protons and
        neutrons. By the time a human heartbeat could have completed, the
        cosmos has gone through more phase transitions than the rest of its
        history combined.
      </p>

      <p data-fade>
        The Particle Age — Chapter 1 of <em>Our Cosmic History</em> — is
        about that astonishing first stretch, from <strong>t = 0</strong> at
        the Big Bang singularity all the way to <strong>380,000 years</strong>{" "}
        later, when the cosmos finally cooled enough for light to stream
        free. Everything we are made of, every force we feel, every
        ingredient of every star — all of it is set during this window.
      </p>

      <PrimordialTimeline client:visible />

      {/* ── Subpage cards ──────────────────────────────────────────── */}
      <header class="mt-24 mb-10" id="subpages">
        <div
          data-fade
          class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.28em] uppercase text-plasma/80 mb-3 flex items-center gap-3"
        >
          <span class="block w-6 h-px bg-plasma/50"></span> four lessons
        </div>
        <h2
          data-fade
          style="--delay: 80ms"
          class="font-serif font-medium text-white tracking-tight leading-[1.05]"
        >
          <span style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.6rem);"
            >Zoom into each act</span
          >
        </h2>
      </header>

      <p data-fade>
        The tour above is the whole picture. The four lessons below each
        spend more time inside a single phase — the forces, the particles,
        the nuclei, and the light.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="max-w-[920px] mx-auto mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 px-2">
      {
        subs.map((s, i) => {
          const isCur = s.current === true;
          return (
            <li>
              <a
                href={s.href}
                data-fade
                style={`--delay: ${i * 60}ms`}
                aria-current={isCur ? "page" : undefined}
                class={`cta-card surface-card${isCur ? "" : " is-link"} block`}
              >
                <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-2 flex-wrap">
                  <span
                    class="font-mono text-[13px] tracking-[0.18em]"
                    style={`color: ${isCur ? "var(--c-accent)" : "rgb(var(--c-accent-rgb) / 0.85)"};`}
                  >
                    {s.id}
                  </span>
                  <span class="font-mono text-[9px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase" style="color: var(--c-text-faint);">
                    {s.tag}
                  </span>
                  {isCur && (
                    <span
                      class="ml-auto font-mono text-[9px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full"
                      style="color: var(--c-accent); border: 1px solid rgb(var(--c-accent-rgb) / 0.45);"
                    >
                      here
                    </span>
                  )}
                </div>
                <div
                  class="font-serif font-medium leading-tight"
                  style="font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.2vw, 1.7rem); color: var(--c-text-strong);"
                >
                  {s.title}
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-[1.55] max-w-[60ch]" style="color: var(--c-text-soft);">
                  {s.tease}
                </p>
              </a>
            </li>
          );
        })
      }
    </ol>

    <div class="max-w-[68ch] mx-auto px-2">
      <div data-fade class="my-16 rule"></div>

      <p data-fade class="text-[16px] italic leading-[1.7] max-w-[60ch]" style="color: var(--c-text-soft);">
        The Particle Age is over before our species can begin to imagine its
        own beginning. Everything that came after — every star, every world,
        every reader of every word — is downstream of these 380,000 years.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
